IaaS (least abstract, most control)
  - AWS EC2
  - Azure VMs
  - Google Compute Engine
  - (You manage OS, runtime, scaling, etc.)

        ↓

CaaS / Container Orchestration
  - Kubernetes (EKS, GKE, AKS, OpenShift)
  - Amazon ECS
  - Nomad
  - (You manage containers, services, scaling, networking)

  - Docker (tooling/runtime, sits here as the *enabler*, not the platform)
    *Docker is not a service layer, but the container tech used by CaaS*

        ↓

PaaS (Application Platform)
  - AWS App Runner
  - Heroku
  - Google App Engine
  - Azure App Service
  - (You deploy an app or image; platform handles infra, scaling, routing)

        ↓

FaaS / Serverless (most abstract)
  - AWS Lambda
  - Azure Functions
  - Google Cloud Functions
  - Cloudflare Workers
  - (You deploy functions; platform runs and scales them per event)